# 🚀 Not Steam

> **The Wikipedia of Games.** A community-driven storefront and game database where knowledge is as valuable as the games themselves.

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
[![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-0.1.0--alpha-blue)]()

## 📖 Overview

**Not Steam** is a hybrid platform that merges the power of a digital distribution service with the open-knowledge architecture of a Wiki. While traditional stores are controlled strictly by publishers, **Not Steam** empowers the players to document, tag, and verify every piece of game data.

### Why "Not Steam"?
* **Crowdsourced Accuracy:** Community-verified hardware benchmarks.
* **Version History:** Track every update, patch note, and stealth-change.
* **Knowledge Economy:** Earn reputation by contributing to the global archives.

---

## ✨ Core Features

### 🛠 The Wiki-Store Hybrid
* **Open-Edit Pages:** Users edit game descriptions, history, and technical specs.
* **Verified Benchmarks:** Real-world performance stats for specific GPU/CPU combos.
* **Version Rollbacks:** Access historical data and previous versions of game entries.

### 🎮 The Launcher (The "Steam" Side)
* **Digital Library:** One-click install and management for your titles.
* **Community Tags:** Hyper-specific tagging (e.g., "Ultrawide Support," "No Microtransactions").
* **User Profiles:** Showcase your library and your "Editor Rank."

